      "message": "Per discussion, we could test as follows:\n\n1. Make this method, and shouldStartClat below, non-static.\n2. In Nat464XlatTest (e.g., assertShouldStartClat), instead of just calling these statically, call makeNat464Xlat and call the method on the resulting object.\n3. Add a method to ConnectivityService.Dependencies called makeNat464Xlat:\n\n    public Nat464Xlat makeNat464Xlat() {\n        return new Nat464Xlat();\n    }\n\nand replace all calls to \"new Nat464Xlat\" with calls to that method.\n4. Add some simple tests to Nat464XlatTest that check that if the property is false the device never starts. I think we can do that by adding a \"protected boolean isCellular464XlatEnabled\" to Nat464Xlat that just returns the system property, and subclass it in Nat464XlatTest with something that can return false.",
